{
  "version": 2,
  "why": "N1: move work to the write path. A load balancer fronts separate post and feed services; publishing stores the post and enqueues a fan-out job; workers push the post_id into every follower's feed list in a feed cache, so a feed load is one cache read plus a batched post lookup. Flaw left: a 40M-follower account creates 40M inserts per post and backs up the queue for everyone (N2), and media still flows through the app.",
